{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2244","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2244","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2244\",\"parent_revision\":\"a8ddfe6ef7365d5f070012e5db0e73146533cd20dcfce465848d89b4a4392fd8\",\"root_revision\":\"a8ddfe6ef7365d5f070012e5db0e73146533cd20dcfce465848d89b4a4392fd8\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Status**: APPROVED-FOR-PLANNING\\n\\n**Functional intent**: AVAILABLE \u2014 add `backlog_find_duplicates(threshold, section, limit)` MCP tool that clusters existing open backlog items into fuzzy-duplicate groups using the already-implemented `find_fuzzy_duplicates` in `parsing.py:481`.\\n\\n**Scope boundaries**: AVAILABLE \u2014 read-only tool, no mutation of any item. Operates only on open (non-skipped) items loaded via `parse_backlog()`. Returns `clusters` list, `total_clusters`, `total_items_examined`.\\n\\n**External interfaces**: AVAILABLE \u2014 `parsing.py:find_fuzzy_duplicates`, `models.py:FUZZY_DUPLICATE_THRESHOLD=0.80`, `models.py:BacklogItem`, `server.py` MCP tool registration pattern (see `backlog_add` / `backlog_list`).\\n\\n**Constraints**: DERIVABLE \u2014 threshold default 0.80 confirmed in `models.py:416`. The clustering algorithm is an O(n\u00b2) pairwise comparison over open items using `SequenceMatcher`. Caller controls threshold and section filter to limit compute cost.\\n\\n**Existing system context**: AVAILABLE \u2014 full codebase present; MCP server pattern clear; `operations.py` and `server.py` are the two modification sites.\\n\\n**Verification expectations**: AVAILABLE \u2014 `research/insights/2026-05-10-awesome-codex-skills-issue-triage-improvements.md` provides a concrete `fastmcp call` command and expected output shape.\\n\\n**Research question answers** (verified from codebase, 2026-05-14):\\n1. `backlog_groom` and `backlog_normalize` perform no duplicate detection. Duplicate detection is strictly create-time only (`_check_for_duplicates` in `backlog_add`).\\n2. `FUZZY_DUPLICATE_THRESHOLD = 0.80` (`models.py:416`). Exposing `threshold` as a caller-controlled parameter (default 0.80) covers both the create-time rejection use case and the softer clustering use case.\\n3. GitHub Issues API has no fuzzy title similarity endpoint. The `duplicate` label exists but requires manual application. Local `difflib.SequenceMatcher` computation is appropriate.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-14)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n8/10 \u2014 The fuzzy-duplicate function exists and is tested at create-time but is dead code for agents working on the existing 318-item open corpus. A bulk triage workflow (`/dh:scan-stale-backlog`, #1136) explicitly depends on this capability to identify and merge duplicates in the same pass as staleness detection. Without this tool, deduplication requires destructive workarounds (`backlog_add` creates items when no duplicate is found) or manual quadratic effort.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: `/dh:scan-stale-backlog` (#1136) cannot deduplicate as part of its bulk triage pass without this tool.\\n- Bottleneck: Any agent or human doing backlog hygiene (deduplicate before grooming) must resort to calling `backlog_add` with each candidate title \u2014 destructive if no duplicate is found \u2014 or do manual comparison.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Exposes existing `find_fuzzy_duplicates` logic to agents without adding new algorithmic complexity.\\n- Enables non-destructive duplicate discovery over the full open corpus.\\n- Unblocks bulk triage workflows that currently cannot identify near-duplicate clusters.\\n- Turns dead code into a live, tested MCP tool surface.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen called with a threshold and optional section filter, the tool loads all open (non-skipped) backlog items, runs pairwise title similarity using `difflib.SequenceMatcher` on normalized titles, groups items that exceed the threshold into clusters, and returns the clusters sorted by member count descending. The tool does not modify any item. If no clusters meet the threshold, it returns an empty `clusters` list with `total_clusters: 0`. The canonical item in each cluster is the one with the highest average similarity to other members (or the lowest issue number as a tiebreak).\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nThe tool is observable when:\\n- `fastmcp call --target backlog_find_duplicates --input-json '{\\\"threshold\\\": 0.75, \\\"limit\\\": 5}'` returns a dict with `clusters`, `total_clusters`, and `total_items_examined` keys.\\n- Each cluster entry contains `cluster_id` (int), `member_count` (int), and `members` (list of `{issue, title, similarity_to_canonical}`).\\n- A call with `threshold=0.99` against diverse titles returns `total_clusters: 0` and `clusters: []`.\\n- A call with `threshold=0.50` against the full open corpus returns `total_items_examined >= 318`.\\n- The tool is registered as `backlog_find_duplicates` in the MCP server tool list returned by `fastmcp list`.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `fastmcp list` against the source backlog server lists `backlog_find_duplicates` as a registered tool.\\n2. `fastmcp call --target backlog_find_duplicates --input-json '{\\\"threshold\\\": 0.75, \\\"limit\\\": 5}'` returns a dict containing keys `clusters`, `total_clusters`, `total_items_examined` with no `error` key.\\n3. Each member in a returned cluster contains `issue` (int or str), `title` (str), and `similarity_to_canonical` (float in [threshold, 1.0]).\\n4. A call with `threshold=0.99` against the live open corpus returns `clusters: []` and `total_clusters: 0` (or a plausible near-zero count \u2014 not an error).\\n5. A call with `threshold=0.50` returns `total_items_examined` equal to the count of open non-skipped items at time of call.\\n6. The tool is marked `readOnlyHint=True` in its `ToolAnnotations`.\\n7. The tool is covered by at least one unit test in `tests/` that exercises the clustering logic without hitting GitHub (using mock or memory-backend items).\\n8. `uv run prek run --files plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py` exits 0 with no linting errors on the modified files.\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/parsing.py:481-516` \u2014 `find_fuzzy_duplicates` implementation |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/models.py:416` \u2014 `FUZZY_DUPLICATE_THRESHOLD = 0.80` |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py:1621-1637` \u2014 `_check_for_duplicates` (sole current caller) |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` \u2014 MCP server; `backlog_add` and `backlog_list` are the pattern templates |\\n| Prior work | `research/insights/2026-05-10-awesome-codex-skills-issue-triage-improvements.md` \u2014 measurable signal, target `fastmcp call` command, expected output shape |\\n| Agent | @dh:backlog-item-groomer \u2014 used this session |\\n| Agent | @dh:codebase-analyzer \u2014 for impact analysis on `operations.py` / `server.py` modification sites |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None (all required infrastructure \u2014 `find_fuzzy_duplicates`, `parse_backlog`, MCP server \u2014 is already present).\\n- Blocks: #1136 (`/dh:scan-stale-backlog`) \u2014 bulk triage duplicate detection requires this tool to be non-destructive.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 the clustering logic reuses `find_fuzzy_duplicates` without modification. Work is: (1) add `find_existing_duplicate_clusters(items, threshold) -> list[dict]` to `operations.py`, (2) add `backlog_find_duplicates` tool handler to `server.py` following the `backlog_list` pattern, (3) write at least one unit test. No new dependencies, no schema changes, no GitHub API calls.\\n\\n## Where This Is Observed\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe repository has 305+ open issues (per `backlog_list` backend report on 2026-05-10). An agent or human triaging this backlog cannot identify near-duplicate clusters among existing items without manually running `backlog_add` with each candidate title \u2014 a destructive workflow because `backlog_add` creates a new item when no duplicate is detected.\\n</div>\\n\\n## User-Provided Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe pattern source is `research/skill-generation-tools/awesome-codex-skills-issue-triage.md` \u2014 Composio's Issue Triage skill cluster duplicates locally with `LINEAR_LIST_ISSUES` followed by an in-memory similarity grouping step. A measurable target end state would be: `fastmcp call ... --target backlog_find_duplicates --input-json '{\\\"threshold\\\": 0.75, \\\"limit\\\": 5}'` returns a `clusters` key whose entries each contain `members: [{issue, title, similarity_to_canonical}]`.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/skill-generation-tools/awesome-codex-skills-issue-triage.md \u2014 pattern: Local Deduplication (cluster duplicates locally)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-10\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **add mcp tool to cluster existing open backlog items into duplicate groups** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Research First\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n? Does `backlog_groom` or `backlog_normalize` already perform any duplicate detection on existing items, or is it strictly create-time?\\n? What threshold value (`FUZZY_DUPLICATE_THRESHOLD`) currently produces useful results on the actual open-issue corpus, and does the same threshold work for clustering as for create-time rejection?\\n? Does the GitHub Issues backend already expose a \\\"find duplicates\\\" capability via labels, search, or graph mutations that should be preferred over local computation?\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- Bulk triage workflows (e.g., the existing `/dh:scan-stale-backlog` tracking item #1136) cannot identify and merge duplicates as part of the same pass that detects staleness.\\n- The fuzzy-duplicate logic is dead code from the perspective of agents working on existing items.\\n- A common backlog hygiene operation (deduplicate before grooming) requires manual quadratic effort.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`find_fuzzy_duplicates(title, items, threshold)` exists in `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/parsing.py:481-516` and uses `difflib.SequenceMatcher` on normalized titles. It is invoked at exactly one callsite \u2014 `_check_for_duplicates` in `operations.py:1621-1637`, which runs only inside `backlog_add` at item-creation time. There is no MCP tool, CLI command, or skill workflow that takes the set of currently open items and returns duplicate clusters.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"01403bba4da4a4f65f39388c0b5abd5148a3f66eec22fa700337f88be6985cdd\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPS_4eA\"}"}